{"id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op.2","title":"Keystream index access assumes KDF output length","description":"File: oscore/src/edhoc/initiator.rs:316-317

Issue: `keystream_2[i]` accesses keystream bytes using an index from `ciphertext_2.enumerate()`. The code assumes `keystream_2.len() >= ciphertext_2.len()` because `edhoc_kdf` was called with `ciphertext_2.len()`, but this is not asserted.

Trigger: If the KDF returns fewer bytes than requested (implementation bug or buffer limit), this will panic with index-out-of-bounds.

Suggested fix: Assert length before the XOR loop:
```rust
assert_eq!(keystream_2.len(), ciphertext_2.len());
// or better, return error:
if keystream_2.len() < ciphertext_2.len() {
    return Err(EdhocError::KeyDerivation);
}
